{
  "abstract": "The Konavle construction gives seven rational entries with twenty Diophantine square conditions; the remaining square leads to elliptic covers over an octic field. Earlier support and local calculations leave six necessary twists, with two-isogeny rank bounds $8,8,8,10,10,10$. We strengthen these bounds to $8,6,6,8,10,6$. A rational-kernel tangent pairing lowers three bounds by two. A full two-descent then proves that the two-Selmer group of the isogenous curve has dimension seven for each of the two twists without known boundary points, giving rank at most six on both. Exact norm representatives, a complete correction space, and local Kummer images certified by the isogeny exact sequence establish the full descent. We also construct the two conjugate nonrational-torsion tangent characters and evaluate them on every admitted full two-Selmer basis class. All resulting pairings with the required class-three torsor vanish. The proofs identify the relevant half-divisors explicitly and account for every finite and infinite place. A compact supplement independently replays the new arithmetic, including local Hensel witnesses and direct Hilbert symbols; the previous unconditional support and two-isogeny certificate is a pinned public prerequisite. Neither target twist has a known nontorsion point or certified global span from this work. Thus the rank threshold for elliptic Chabauty is improved, but no twist is excluded, no rational-point classification is claimed, and the septuple problem remains open.",
